              <tr>
                <td bgcolor="whitesmoke" valign="top" width="100" nowrap><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><b>Huggs Enkisses</b></font></td>
                <td bgcolor="whitesmoke" valign="top" width="100%"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><small>Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;06/16/2004&nbsp;: 02:00:49 AM</small><hr size="1"><span class="spnMessageText"> Before I ask you to answer these questions I figured it would only be fair that I answer them for you....<br />I have four characters I currently play, Ccogrl, Huggs, Beautiless, and Mindycandy.  They are in order listed above, 58, 55, 31, and 12 at this point.   I have been playing EQ for 5 years since it came out pretty much.  My husband plays too.  My friends pretty much play EQ with me.  My non everquest friends don't really understand it and have no desire to learn anything about EQ.  In the past I would stay up till about midnight with raids not so much anymore.  I don't get much time to play and when I do get time it is very limited sad to say.  Question 5 isn't one I can answer totally since my husband does play.  If he didn't I would probably quit if he asked me too.  As far as taking away from my family, no it doesn't really since, his dad and his sister and his brother-in-law all play.  No kids for us yet.  Heck his family is pretty much playing at different levels.  We do make time for non-EQ family time though.  I generally play for maybe 10 hours a week now but I was at a point where I would play for 20 or maybe even 30 hours a week.  I don't feel it has a negative impact on my life.  I feel it allows me to escape stress, others find different ways then I do.  When I first started to play EQ it was to spend time with someone that I really thought I wanted to spend the rest of my life with, boy was I wrong.  EQ did however lead me to the man I married.  He and I talked for a year as friends on line before ever meeting.   As I progress ever so slowly in levels most of my friends that I started the game with have passed me.  I look forward to the days when I can join them again but, till this paper gets done my EQ time will have to be limited.  <br /><br />Here is the Survey:<br /><br />1.  How many characters do you currently play?  What are thier levels?  How long have you played?<br /><br />2.  Does your spouse play with you?<br /><br />3. What do your friends think of EQ?  Do you play amongst a group of friends you socialize with regularly outside of the game?<br /><br />4.  How many hours a week do you usually play EQ?  Do you find yourself up late at night for guild raids or events?<br /><br />5.  If your spouse doesn't play the game, does he/she voice an opinion of the game?  Do you feel you spend enough time with him/her since they don't play?  <br /><br />6.  Do you feel the game takes away from doing things with your family?<br /><br />7.  Do you know of anyone who has experienced anything positive from playing EQ? <br /><br />8.  Do you honestly feel you could walk away from the game if you had too?<br /><br />9.  Do you remember what caused you to want to play the game?<br /><br />10.  What are your thoughts of all the bad press EQ gets because people claim it is addictive? <br /><br />11.  Your name or contact information so my professor can verify my survey source if she so wishes.  (she may want to check to make sure you are a real EQ player) <br /><br />Thanks for taking the time to fill out my survey.  If you wish to email your answers to me you can do that too.  <a href="mailto:Ccogrl2001@yahoo.com">Ccogrl2001@yahoo.com</a> <br /><br />1000 Thanks again guys</span></font></td>
              </tr>
