 nowrap><b><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2">Crazyfrog</font></b></td>
                <td bgcolor="darkgray" valign="top"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><small>Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;06/29/2004&nbsp;: 08:27:14 AM</small><hr size="1"><span class="spnMessageText"> 1. How many characters do you currently play? What are thier levels? How long have you played?<br /><font color="blue"><ul><br /><li>59 Warrior  </li><br /><li>47 Bard  </li><br /><li>29 Enchanter  </li><br /><li>26 Druid </li><br /></ul><br />I have been playing for about 4 years (as a casual player mostly)<br /></font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />2. Does your spouse play with you?<br /><br /><font color="blue">Yes she does occasionnaly.  She has been quite busy with school and work.</font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />3. What do your friends think of EQ? Do you play amongst a group of friends you socialize with regularly outside of the game?<br /><br /><font color="blue">Most of my friends think it is a waste of time and it's taking away from real life.  Some of them do play and love it, others want to play but dont have enough money.</font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />4. How many hours a week do you usually play EQ? Do you find yourself up late at night for guild raids or events?<br /><br /><font color="blue">I usually play about 3 hours per day(if I can) and 10 on weekend days which makes up a total of 25 hours per week.  I do occasionaly find myself staying up late for raids or events.</font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />5. If your spouse doesn't play the game, does he/she voice an opinion of the game? Do you feel you spend enough time with him/her since they don't play? <br /><br /><font color="blue">As she does not play often because of school and work, she does beleive that I play too much and it takes away from our relationship.  But recently, we took time away from work and everything else and took a trip! <img src="http://www.eciunbroken.com/forums/images/icon_smile.gif" border="0" alt="" title="" align="middle" /></font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />6. Do you feel the game takes away from doing things with your family?<br /><br /><font color="blue">Yes, when I have free time I usually start playing EverQuest rather than taking a trip to visit my family.</font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />7. Do you know of anyone who has experienced anything positive from playing EQ? <br /><br /><font color="blue">There are so many positive things that come from EverQuest such as:<br /><ul><br /><li>Communication Skills (Learning English, learning the correct spelling of words, communicating with others etc..)  </li><br /><li>Typing Skills  </li><br /><li>Leadership Skills  </li><br /><li>Entertainment (no need for Cable TV, saves money if its your main form of entertainment)</li><br /><li>Stress releif</li><br /></ul><br /></font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />8. Do you honestly feel you could walk away from the game if you had to?<br /><br /><font color="blue">Yes I beleive that if I had to walk away from the game, I would.</font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />9. Do you remember what caused you to want to play the game?<br /><br /><font color="blue">I have always been into computer games and a friend was telling me about this new game called EverQuest and he was telling me about his adventures in the game at work.  Every day that he told me more about the game, the more I wanted it.  I have been playing ever since I turned of age to get a credit card.</font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />10. What are your thoughts of all the bad press EQ gets because people claim it is addictive? <br /><br /><font color="blue">I think it's just to prove how good the game is and that it is a sort of warning to anyone that wants to try it.  I beleive it also raises individuals' curiosity about the game which brings in more people to play.</font id="blue"><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br />11. Your name or contact information so my professor can verify my survey source if she so wishes. (she may want to check to make sure you are a real EQ player) <br /><br /><font color="blue">My name is Paul and my email address is <a href="mailto:warrior_the_man@hotmail.com">warrior_the_man@hotmail.com</a></font id="blue"></span></font></td>
