                <td bgcolor="darkgray" valign="top"
 nowrap><b><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2">Daque Attaque</font></b></td>
                <td bgcolor="darkgray" valign="top"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><small>Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;06/27/2004&nbsp;: 4:39:48 PM</small><hr size="1"><span class="spnMessageText"> 1. How many characters do you currently play? What are thier levels? How long have you played?<br />-- 5 toons for me Daque (54 ranger) Shimi (45 rogue) Spankey (26 shaman) Daquey (26 beastlord) Descus (24 Enchanter) - I started EQ about 6 months before Kunark came out.<br /> <br />2. Does your spouse play with you? <br />-- I'm not married yet, but my girlfriend of 2 years does not play...<br /><br />3. What do your friends think of EQ? Do you play amongst a group of friends you socialize with regularly outside of the game? <br />--When I started EQ I did, my friends got me into it actually. But as time went by they got sick of it and we all kinda just stopped playing (that was around lvl 51 or soon Daque)- as for now, I don't have any RL friends that play, the old friends that quit on me now play War Craft or BF1942/Vietnam - my other close friends and girlfriend kind of get annoyed when i  tell them I'm playing.<br /><br />4. How many hours a week do you usually play EQ? Do you find yourself up late at night for guild raids or events? <br />--I'd say I'm on between 15 and 25 hours a week, MOSTLY late at night because I'm usually busy hanging with the gang during the day and night.<br /><br />5. If your spouse doesn't play the game, does he/she voice an opinion of the game? Do you feel you spend enough time with him/her since they don't play? <br />--The G/F "-hates-" EQ but she is ok because I don't let it interfere with RL. In fact you usually see me logging so I can go see her<br /><br />6. Do you feel the game takes away from doing things with your family?<br />--It used to - that's the main reason I took a year long break and then another 4 month or so one. Now that I'm in college I make sure I treat like a game instead of a 2nd life (which is very easy to do)<br /><br />7. Do you know of anyone who has experienced anything positive from playing EQ? <br />--I just play to get my share of RPG action - as far as stories go, my friends even thought they don't play anymore still have lasting RL friendships with people they met on EQ (myself included)<br /><br />8. Do you honestly feel you could walk away from the game if you had too?<br />--If i needed to yes, but so far I keep finding excuses to come back and have fun<br /><br />9. Do you remember what caused you to want to play the game?<br />--peer pressure, plain and simple. my friends told me it was great so i asked for it for Xmas and yay! here I am.<br /><br />10. What are your thoughts of all the bad press EQ gets because people claim it is addictive?<br />--I say play at your own risk, It's players that make it addictive I don't think Sony or Verant wanted this to "pull a marlboro" so to say. It's just like anything else that can become more if you don't control yourself (what does the surgeon general have to say? We should be hearing from him/her soon). Just don't forget that you're looking at a computer screen and still need to eat and get out and make a living, or get an education. <br /><br />11. Your name or contact information so my professor can verify my survey source if she so wishes. (she may want to check to make sure you are a real EQ player) <br />-- Robert Lara   <img src="http://www.eciunbroken.com/forums/images/icon_smile_blackeye.gif" border="0" alt="" title="" align="middle" />  <a href="mailto:RaftyBob@hotmail.com">RaftyBob@hotmail.com</a> <br /></span></font></td>
              </tr>
