                <td bgcolor="whitesmoke" valign="top"
 nowrap><b><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2">Kanein Encanto</font></b></td>
                <td bgcolor="whitesmoke" valign="top"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><small>Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;06/27/2004&nbsp;: 11:38:11 AM</small><hr size="1"><span class="spnMessageText"> Almost forgot, sorry Huggs <img src="http://www.eciunbroken.com/forums/images/bigeyes2_125.gif" border="0" alt="" title="" align="middle" /><br /><br />1. How many characters do you currently play? What are thier levels? How long have you played?<br /><br />Primarily I play one character, Kanein, Lv 65 Enchanter, usually don't play alts much, if at all. If I remember right, I started mid-2001.<br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />2. Does your spouse play with you?<br /><br />N/A<br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />3. What do your friends think of EQ? Do you play amongst a group of friends you socialize with regularly outside of the game?<br /><br />I've never been one to have many friends to start with, but a few instead. Before they moved out of town 2 or so years ago, they seemed interested, but didn't have the computer / connection to play. We were content to play Magic: The Gathering. As for my friends at work, I don't really talk about EQ at work much, if at all.<br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />4. How many hours a week do you usually play EQ? Do you find yourself up late at night for guild raids or events?<br /><br />Probably near 30 hour. Ever since my last job, I find I'm really not tired enough to fall asleep until around midnight, but I don't remember ever trying to stay up for a raid or event beyond that. I usually play with that end-time in mind. Friday / Saturday nights are a different story though.<br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />5. If your spouse doesn't play the game, does he/she voice an opinion of the game? Do you feel you spend enough time with him/her since they don't play? <br /><br />N/A<br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />6. Do you feel the game takes away from doing things with your family?<br /><br />No more than work tends to in my opinion.<br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />7. Do you know of anyone who has experienced anything positive from playing EQ? <br /><br />I myself have come away with something positive from playing EQ, as I've continued to play, I've become able to type by touch (without looking at the keyboard) and my type-rate has been on the rise also. It's actually how I landed the job I have right now, a data entry position. <br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />8. Do you honestly feel you could walk away from the game if you had too?<br /><br />If I had do, I'm sure I could, but I still enjoy exploring, and the conversations. When I don't feel like playing, I don't think much about not playing that day.<br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />9. Do you remember what caused you to want to play the game?<br /><br />Happened upon an article on it, and it interested me, so I decided to buy it and give it a try, since I enjoyed other RPG style games as well. (Namely Final Fantasy, and to some degree Magic: The Gathering is an RPG too)<br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />10. What are your thoughts of all the bad press EQ gets because people claim it is addictive? <br /><br />I feel a bit on the angry side, in this day and age it seems saying that something is addictive is a quick way to take the blame of one's shoulders for making a bad decision. (IE people have in the past made claims that shopping, or fast food are addictive) I've been a video game 'addict' since the old 8-bit Nintendo system was out, I just enjoy games, video or not. <br /><br /><hr noshade size="1"><br /><br />11. Your name or contact information so my professor can verify my survey source if she so wishes. (she may want to check to make sure you are a real EQ player) <br />Jonathan Bottger<br />Best mailbox to use would be <a href="mailto:Kanein_of_eci@hotmail.com,">Kanein_of_eci@hotmail.com,</a> I haven't seen any spam in that box yet, unlike my other two.<br />If he wants to contact in-game, just be sure he lets me know who he is when he (or his assistant) sends a tell. <img src="http://www.eciunbroken.com/forums/images/icon_smile.gif" border="0" alt="" title="" align="middle" /><br /><br /></span></font></td>
              </tr>
