                <td bgcolor="darkgray" valign="top"
 nowrap><b><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2">Vorgus</font></b></td>
                <td bgcolor="darkgray" valign="top"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><small>Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;06/21/2004&nbsp;: 4:26:12 PM</small><hr size="1"><span class="spnMessageText"> 1. How many characters do you currently play? What are thier levels? How long have you played?<br /><br />I've played many many different characters but those I've put alot of time into: Vorgus lvl 65, Arimoon lvl 57, Frumps lvl 53, Takkara lvl 52, Redwin lvl 45. I've played since soon after the Kunark expansion was released - bout 4-5 years ago?<br /><br />2. Does your spouse play with you?<br /><br />Yes<br /><br />3. What do your friends think of EQ? Do you play amongst a group of friends you socialize with regularly outside of the game?<br /><br />Depending on which friends you ask, some friends play the game, and those who don't really don't understand what it's all about. I have one friend who plays and we socialize pretty regularly in RL (Mcmassacre). Also, I've met about 12 of my "EQ buddies" in RL when my wife and I threw an EQ party in St. Louis last year.<br /><br />4. How many hours a week do you usually play EQ? Do you find yourself up late at night for guild raids or events?<br /><br />In my prime I played probably 30+ hours a week. Nowadays it's dwindled to 6-8 hours max. In my prime I was known to stay up til dawn, lately 12-2am has been my limit and haven't been able to participate much in guild raids or events as of yet.<br /><br />5. If your spouse doesn't play the game, does he/she voice an opinion of the game? Do you feel you spend enough time with him/her since they don't play? <br /><br />My wife plays EQ (Goldleif)<br /><br />6. Do you feel the game takes away from doing things with your family?<br /><br />In the past when I played *alot* more yes, sometimes we felt that EQ took away from family time but not anymore.<br /><br />7. Do you know of anyone who has experienced anything positive from playing EQ? <br /><br />Yes, me. I've met alot of great people playing the game and EQ is a great way to relax and make friends. I know many other people who've had positive experiences from playing EQ, in that it's relaxing, fun and a good way to meet people in-game and in RL.<br /><br />8. Do you honestly feel you could walk away from the game if you had too?<br /><br />Yes<br /><br />9. Do you remember what caused you to want to play the game?<br /><br />I'm a HUGE roleplaying game fan, both pencil-and-paper, PC, whatever. I started playing Dungeons & Dragons back in 1984 and have always been into fantasy novels, sci-fi, horror and games. A friend suggested that I try it and wham....for a long time I considered EQ to be something akin to D&D online.<br /><br />10. What are your thoughts of all the bad press EQ gets because people claim it is addictive? <br /><br />EQ is only addictive to people who allow it to be addictive, so I feel that EQ *can* be addictive to some people if they let it or if they have addictive personalities.<br /><br />Sean Simmons == <a href="mailto:vorgus2k@yahoo.com">vorgus2k@yahoo.com</a> == junkmail shall be immediately slain with extreme predjudice!!<br /><br /><br /><br /><br /><br /></span></font></td>
