                <td bgcolor="whitesmoke" valign="top"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><small>Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;06/16/2004&nbsp;: 10:55:24 AM</small><hr size="1"><span class="spnMessageText"> 1.  2 active toons/1 mule....65 shm; 56 war; 1 bard (mule)....started playing in 4/2003.<br /><br />2.  No<br /><br />3.  My good friends play EQ as well but is cutting back due to real life obligations.<br /><br />4.  I play quite a bit, maybe 25+ hours?  And yes, I do stay up late to raid.....<img src="http://www.eciunbroken.com/forums/images/drunk_125.gif" border="0" alt="" title="" align="middle" /><br /><br />5.  My wife doesn't play but understands that I need something to occupy my time since she is overseas working at the moment.  She doesn't have to worry about me "out and about" since she can either find me at work or online all the frigging time!  hehe <br /><br />6.  Not really.  My cousin, brother, and sister-in-law all play this game.  Great way for us to keep in touch with each other on almost a daily basis.<br /><br />7.  This is a difficult question to answer since everyone's definition of positive is very different.  My opinion is that EQ is a good distraction from real life.  It is a great way to escape reality for that brief moment in the day when you log on.  The problem comes when people cannot distinguish reality from fantasy.  But then again, this is true for anything, i.e. books, movies, plays, etc.<br /><br />8.  Yes....but will only do so when I have become bored with the game.<br /><br />9.  My friends and I got bored of the Diablo series and wanted something similar.  That's how we got started in EQ.<br /><br />10.  Never encountered any bad publicity about EQ.<br /><br />11.  <a href="mailto:RLIUJR@YAHOO.COM">RLIUJR@YAHOO.COM</a></span></font></td>
