                <td bgcolor="whitesmoke" valign="top"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><small>Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;06/16/2004&nbsp;: 09:40:49 AM</small><hr size="1"><span class="spnMessageText"> 1. How many characters do you currently play? What are thier levels? How long have you played?<br />Valeris 64,Bizcat 30,Angelwar 45,Aeragorne 39, Sweetbuffs 30, Barisha 17, Niania 17. I started in 2001.<br />2. Does your spouse play with you? Not applicable<br /><br />3. What do your friends think of EQ? Do you play amongst a group of friends you socialize with regularly outside of the game? I talk with friends at work who ask about the game and most have heard and/or seen the effects of EQ with family or friends. So most of the feedback on EQ is negative, at least that I've heard.<br />No, most of my friends are completing their residency and even when they want to play they cannot due to school.<br />4. How many hours a week do you usually play EQ? Do you find yourself up late at night for guild raids or events? About 36 hours a week. Yes, I do stay up once in a while, not often. I dont want to be at work the next day half asleep. Its a very demanding job.<br /><br />5. If your spouse doesn't play the game, does he/she voice an opinion of the game? Do you feel you spend enough time with him/her since they don't play? Not applicable...If I ever get married again,or get a boyfriend, I would most likely not play much. <br /><br />6. Do you feel the game takes away from doing things with your family? Sometimes yes. I have been taking the time lately to leave the game and spend more time with family.<br /><br />7. Do you know of anyone who has experienced anything positive from playing EQ? Yes a few freinds on the game have met and are happily married or are very good RL friends. I have in my own little way. I think it is a better way to spend my time rather than sitting on a couch watching whatever. I also use the game to communicate with my oldest son who is married and far from home. Phone bills are rough :)<br /><br />8. Do you honestly feel you could walk away from the game if you had too? Yes ..I wouldnt like to but yes.<br /><br />9. Do you remember what caused you to want to play the game? My oldest son said "Hey mom this game is soooooooooo cool" :)<br /><br />10. What are your thoughts of all the bad press EQ gets because people claim it is addictive? <br />It is addictive. However, so are a lot of other things.<br />11. Your name or contact information so my professor can verify my survey source if she so wishes. (she may want to check to make sure you are a real EQ player) <a href="mailto:Valeris777@hotmail.com">Valeris777@hotmail.com</a><br /></span></font></td>
