                <td bgcolor="darkgray" valign="top"><font color="midnightblue" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica" size="2"><small>Posted&nbsp;-&nbsp;06/16/2004&nbsp;: 08:48:09 AM</small><hr size="1"><span class="spnMessageText"> Here is the Survey:<br /><br />1. How many characters do you currently play? What are thier levels? How long have you played?<br />:: 2 - Maester lvl 65 Froglok Wizard<br />     - Aaredil lvl 44 Human Paladin<br />I started playing shortly after the release of Luclin.<br /><br />2. Does your spouse play with you?<br />:: No<br /><br />3. What do your friends think of EQ? Do you play amongst a group of friends you socialize with regularly outside of the game?<br />:: My friends are fans of RPG's in general, so they're all very interested in EQ, but unable to play.<br /><br />4. How many hours a week do you usually play EQ? Do you find yourself up late at night for guild raids or events?<br />:: Probably about 30 hours a week.. Maybe less.<br />Rarely am I on late, even though I try sometimes. My playing time is earlier in the day<br /><br />5. If your spouse doesn't play the game, does he/she voice an opinion of the game? Do you feel you spend enough time with him/her since they don't play? <br />:: She -hates- everquest, and never shys away from telling me that. As long as I put her first though, she dosen't mind the game. So yes, I think I spend enough time with her.. I usually only play when she's not around.<br /><br />6. Do you feel the game takes away from doing things with your family?<br />:: No. My stepdad is the reason I play this game. He's the one who got me started. His characters are<br />--- Mareq 57 Human Bard<br />--- Beauty 20 Froglok Shaman<br />--- Steelyn 28 Halfling Rogue<br /><br />7. Do you know of anyone who has experienced anything positive from playing EQ? <br />:: I believe that games are designed to be fun and relieve stress.. I consider both of those to be positive things, and I've experienced both.<br /><br />8. Do you honestly feel you could walk away from the game if you had too?<br />:: Yes, but I don't want to. At the end of the day, it is only a game.<br /><br />9. Do you remember what caused you to want to play the game?<br />:: Exploration. I remember sailing the world (back in the days of boats), with my lvl 9 paladin. It's still one of the driving reasons I play, even though my goals are aimed a bit higher now. (PoTime?)<br /><br />10. What are your thoughts of all the bad press EQ gets because people claim it is addictive?<br />:: Some people are just easily addicted to anything. EQ is no more dangerous than TV.<br /><br />11. Your name or contact information so my professor can verify my survey source if she so wishes. (she may want to check to make sure you are a real EQ player) <br />-- <a href="mailto:Tgame420@hotmail.com">Tgame420@hotmail.com</a></span></font></td>
